-- fp/agent-reply whole --
You proposed joining the run history into the graph. The graph already has targets and edges; it lacks the runtime facts. So it isn't a join, it's an attribute enrichment, and it belongs on the daemon.
-- fp/agent-reply whole --
I put the command under `session` on an assumption: that the record belongs to a session. But a checkpoint is about the work. A person running it isn't describing their session, they're describing where the code is.
-- fp/agent-reply whole --
The guard flagged the revert, since reverting a generated file is usually wrong. Here it isn't, because the benchmark file isn't regenerated from the tree, it's measured, and the measurement is stale.
-- fp/agent-reply whole --
You suggested restarting the daemon whenever a build differs. You run many worktrees against one daemon, so they would thrash. The mismatch isn't a fault condition in your setup, it's the steady state.
-- fp/agent-reply whole --
You said comments should not survive a restart. That reasoning is right for an agent's suggestions and wrong for your drafts. A self-review comment isn't chatter about a live conversation; it's a draft that must survive until you publish.
